prts.feedbackvariables:
/* Input verification - Check whether the counter example input is a matrix, then check whether it is of dimension 2x2. Note that if the input is not a matrix, the dimension verification always fails. It is important that the PRT stops if the input is not a matrix. */
isInputMatrix : matrixp(ansMatrix);
M : if isInputMatrix then ansMatrix else ident(1);
isInputDimension : is((length(M) = 2) and (length(transpose(M)) = 2));
okayInput : isInputMatrix and isInputDimension;

/* Check whether the example supplied by the student is indeed correct. If the student answered that the statement is true, then the variable exampleChecksOut is automatically set to be false. */
/*replace "0=0" with logical test returning true/false */
exampleChecksOut : if ansTF then false else is(not(M[1,2]=0 and M[2,1]=0) and ((M.M)[1,2]=0 and (M.M)[2,1]=0))
